# =============================================================
#  State of Mind RP — .gitignore
#  Goal: track ONLY the resources + the config the server needs
#  to run. Everything that is a build artifact, runtime-generated,
#  machine-specific, or secret is ignored so that a `git pull` on
#  the VM never overwrites the live server binaries or data.
# =============================================================

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  FXServer build artifacts (the "Server" / artifact folder)
#  These are the FXServer binaries themselves (build 25770 etc).
#  They are downloaded per-build on the VM and must never be in git
#  or a pull will clobber the running server's executables.
# -------------------------------------------------------------
/Server/
# In case the artifact folder is ever named differently:
**/FXServer.exe
**/citizen/
**/alpine/

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  txAdmin / runtime caches (regenerated on every boot)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
txData/**/cache/
txData/**/.replxx_history
**/cache/files/

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  txAdmin runtime data, player database & logs (machine-specific,
#  changes constantly, and contains player PII)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
txData/default/data/
txData/default/logs/
txData/**/logs/
crashes/
**/crashes/
*.log

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  Secrets / credentials (NEVER commit these)
#  - admins.json holds txAdmin password hashes + identifiers
#  - config.json holds the DB password / txAdmin secrets
#  - TLS keys + server tokens
#  server.cfg is now IGNORED because it holds sv_licenseKey +
#  steam_webApiKey + mysql_connection_string. A redacted
#  server.cfg.example is tracked instead — copy it to server.cfg
#  and fill in real secrets on the VM.
# -------------------------------------------------------------
txData/admins.json
txData/default/config.json
**/server.cfg
!**/server.cfg.example
# Backups of server.cfg also hold the live secrets — never commit them
**/server.cfg.bkp
**/server.cfg.backup
**/server.cfg.bak

# som.cfg is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds boot order, convars and
# permissions, none of which are secret, so a push carries the config to the
# VPS instead of it being hand copied and drifting.
*.bkp
*.bak
**/server-tls.key
**/server-tls.crt
**/server-monitor-token.key
*.pem

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  Streamed / heavy binary game assets that bloat the repo.
#  These are what pushed the repo past 13GB and made GitHub pushes
#  time out, so they are ignored. Keep them on disk / host elsewhere.
# -------------------------------------------------------------
# The whole streamed-asset resource tree (brackets are literal dir
# names, so they must be escaped or git treats them as a char class):
**/\[assets-streams\]/
# Any stream folder under any resource:
**/stream/
# Heavy binary asset formats wherever they appear:
*.ytd
*.yft
*.ydr
*.ybn
*.ydd
*.rpf
*.ymt
*.ymap
*.ytyp
*.awc
*.ypt
*.ynv

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  Node / build dependency trees (regenerated via npm install)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules/

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  Claude Code skills (local reference docs, not needed on server)
# -------------------------------------------------------------
skills/

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  AI development session reports (audits, fix logs, rundowns) —
#  useful in the moment, not meant to be permanent repo docs
# -------------------------------------------------------------
/rundown.md
/STARTUP_FIXES.md
/SECURITY_AUDIT.md

# -------------------------------------------------------------
#  OS / editor junk
# -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*.tmp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace
txData/FiveMBasicServerCFXDefault_3A7DA0.base/resources/\[standalone\]/Lennox-DoorCreator/lennox-doorcreator-prompt.md
CLAUDE.md
som-framework-rebuild-prompt.md

# LCPDFR police/EMS pack, dropped into the repo for wiring (plan's "yours" list).
# Streamed binaries and livery templates are copied to the server by hand and
# never committed. The two dlc.rpf files alone are 480MB and 295MB, and GitHub
# hard rejects anything over 100MB, which is why this route was abandoned once
# already. *.rpf is covered above; this covers the 96MB of sign templates,
# ELS configs and screenshots alongside them.
/Vehicles/
